  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 18,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "('Let $X$ be a smooth projective variety defined over a number field $K$, and '\n",
      " 'let $f\\\\colon X\\\\dashrightarrow X$ be a dominant rational self-map defined '\n",
      " 'over $K$. Define the (first) dynamical degree of $f$ by\\n'\n",
      " '$$\\\\delta_f \\\\;=\\\\; \\\\lim_{n\\\\to\\\\infty}\\\\bigl(\\\\deg(f^n)\\\\bigr)^{1/n},$$\\n'\n",
      " 'where $\\\\deg(f^n)$ denotes the degree of $f^n$ with respect to a fixed ample '\n",
      " 'divisor on $X$ (the limit is independent of this choice). For a point $P\\\\in '\n",
      " 'X(\\\\overline{K})$ whose forward orbit $\\\\{P,f(P),f^2(P),\\\\dots\\\\}$ is '\n",
      " 'well-defined, define the arithmetic degree of $f$ at $P$ by\\n'\n",
      " '$$\\\\alpha_f(P) \\\\;=\\\\; \\\\limsup_{n\\\\to\\\\infty} '\n",
      " '\\\\max\\\\bigl(1,\\\\,h_X(f^n(P))\\\\bigr)^{1/n},$$\\n'\n",
      " 'where $h_X$ is a Weil height on $X$ associated to an ample divisor.\\n'\n",
      " '\\n'\n",
      " 'The following are known/conjectured for points $P\\\\in X(\\\\overline{K})$:\\n'\n",
      " '\\\\begin{itemize}\\n'\n",
      " '\\\\item[(A)] (Existence/upper bound) The limsup defining $\\\\alpha_f(P)$ is in '\n",
      " 'fact a limit, and $\\\\alpha_f(P)\\\\le \\\\delta_f$.\\n'\n",
      " '\\\\item[(B)] (Equality conjecture) If the forward orbit of $P$ under $f$ is '\n",
      " 'well-defined and Zariski dense in $X$, then $\\\\alpha_f(P)=\\\\delta_f$.\\n'\n",
      " '\\\\end{itemize}\\n'\n",
      " '\\n'\n",
      " 'Question: To what extent do statements (A) and (B) remain valid if one '\n",
      " 'restricts the point $P$ to lie in $X(K)$, the set of $K$-rational points of '\n",
      " '$X$, rather than allowing $P\\\\in X(\\\\overline{K})$? In particular, is the '\n",
      " 'analogue of (A) known unconditionally for $P\\\\in X(K)$, and for which '\n",
      " 'classes of varieties $X$ and rational self-maps $f$ does the analogue of (B) '\n",
      " 'hold for $P\\\\in X(K)$ with Zariski dense $f$-orbit?')\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
